From ad2212000943ac4285afcf6e942754329bf2cf44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Pulipaka <adipu@utexas.edu>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:22:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/16] Metal: one-world-per-thread sparse L'DL factor and
 solve; skip no-op gravcomp / tendon-damping launches

- _factor_i_sparse on Metal: the whole L'DL factorization of a world in one thread (one launch instead of a
  copy, one launch per tree level and the diagonal); same updates in the same level order, updates of a
  level that hit the same row applied in list order instead of atomically (float rounding only; bitwise
  equal to the level-parallel path on CPU).
- _solve_LD_sparse on Metal: the fused solve ran one lane per world in one-thread threadgroups (the CPU
  fallback, dim_block 1); now one world per thread in full threadgroups (BlockDim.sparse_ldl_serial, 32),
  the same operation sequence, bit for bit.
- passive: the gravity-compensation kernel ((nworld, nbody-1, nv) threads) is launched only when a body
  has gravcomp at put_model time or body_gravcomp is batched (Model.has_gravcomp), as MuJoCo C's ngravcomp.
- derivative: the tendon-damping qDeriv kernel is launched only when the model has tendons.
MetalSim G1 flat (m_dense_max 0, register Cholesky 48): training loop 46.8K -> 52.5K env-steps/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
